<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6545] Failure during Ignite Service.cancel() can break normal shutdown process.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6545</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;org.apache.ignite.services.Service is a public interface, but Ignite fully relies it&apos;s cacel method is implemented properly and throws no errors.&lt;br/&gt;
However, if one of services fails on cancel(), then other services may not be stopped properly as well as their executor pools.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We should wrap Service.cancel method in try-catch to avoid this.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
